@ 29.1.1.1.3 - Proto-Athabaskan to Beaver
# citation: Whimemsz, from Krauss, Michael and Victor Golla (1981), “Northern Athapaskan Languages”. Handbook of North American Indians, Vol. 6 (Subarctic), 67 – 85
	P:[-voice]S > P:[-voice]:[+laryngeal] (most often back to 3, however)
	{P:[-voice]Š,P:[-voice]Šʷ} > P:[-voice]S
	[+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo, +click] > P:[-voice]Š [+ cons, - fr, + bk, + hi, - lo]
	P:[-voice] > P:[-voice]Š / :{ _i, in the:[+back]ritish Columbian dialect, _e, in the:[+back]ritish Columbian dialect, _u, in the:[+back]ritish Columbian dialect }:
